      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A sleepy opening night gave way to a sturdier response, and that's the story in Toronto right now - sorting itself out fast. <strong>The Leafs' 2-1 win over the Islanders on Sep. 30</strong> steadied a team that had dropped a 3-2 decision to the Canadiens a night earlier, and it leaves them 1-1-0, second in the Atlantic with 2 points, one game back. That's early, yes, but it matters: good clubs stop the wobble before it becomes a habit. The bigger backdrop is off the ice - Rogers now owns MLSE outright, a clean sweep that puts a new power structure over a franchise that has known too many false dawns. The Leafs need their top scorers to keep the blade sharp and their injured depth to heal. <strong>Next comes Ottawa on Saturday at 7 p.m. - another test of whether this surge is real.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated October 2, 2026"
      },
