        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The first drumbeat of Raptors camp is belief, and it's beating through Jamal Shead. <strong>Toronto locked up its heart-and-soul guard on a three-year extension</strong>, a clean, sensible piece of business that says the club knows exactly who it wants in the room when the real games begin. Preseason or not, this is the right kind of noise: no panic, no drama, just a young guard who earned trust the hard way and a front office willing to pay for it. The Raptors open with Miami on Saturday, then the season proper arrives Oct. 21 against Chicago. For now, the picture is still being painted - projected roles, final cuts, and how quickly the new pieces stop looking new. <strong>Watch Shead, and watch the first rotation experiments against the Heat.</strong>",
