        "body": "The Commanders have spent the week walking a tightrope - healthy enough to dream, fragile enough to flinch. <strong>Jayden Daniels returned to practice as a limited participant with his elbow still under a watchful eye</strong>, and that is the hinge on which Sunday turns. Washington sits 1-2, third in the NFC East, one game back, and the 33-31 escape over Seattle gave this team a pulse after the rough October start. Daniels' status remains uncertain, so Marcus Mariota is waiting in the wings if the franchise quarterback cannot go. Either way, the offense must sharpen fast in London, where the Colts arrive at 1-2 and the air will feel more like a test than a spectacle. <strong>What matters now is whether Daniels is cleared by Sunday morning - and whether Washington can bank a second straight win if he isn't.</strong>",
